        "original_id": "9c38f6de-bede-5a82-a70c-810528cd7e98",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chas Chandler, John Constantine, Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, John Totleben, Jamie Delano, Philip Bond\n- Companies: DC Comics, Vertigo\n- Products: Chas Chandler (comics), John Constantine, Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood, Northlanders, The Saga of the Swamp Thing\n- Roles: antihero, sidekick, cab driver, friend, writer, illustrator, creators\n\nFacts:\n- John Constantine first appeared in DC Comics in The Saga of the Swamp Thing No. 25, dated June 1984.\n- Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, and John Totleben created John Constantine.\n- John Constantine is a fictional antihero who appears in comic books published by DC Comics and its Vertigo imprint.\n- Chas Chandler is John Constantine's closest and longest-surviving friend, and Chas Chandler acts as his sidekick and cab driver.\n- Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood was written by Jamie Delano, illustrated by Philip Bond, and features John Constantine several decades after most of his series continuity.\n- Northlanders is an American comic book series published by DC Comics under its Vertigo imprint.",
